  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n( (11)/(2) )¹² times ( (2)/(11) )² times ( (11)/(2) )¹⁶ = ( (2)/(11) )⁹m ⁺⁹ \n\n**Formula used:**\n\na^m × a^n = am ⁺ ⁿ\n\n(a/b)^-n = (b/a)^n\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n( (11)/(2) )¹² times ( (2)/(11) )² times ( (11)/(2) )¹⁶ = ( (2)/(11) )⁹m ⁺⁹ \n\n⇒ Combine terms with the same base:\n\n⇒ ( (11)/(2) )¹² ⁺ ¹⁶ × ((2)/(11))²\n\n⇒ ( (11)/(2) )¹² ⁺ ¹⁶ × ((2)/(11))²\n\n⇒ ( (2)/(11) )⁻²⁸× ((2)/(11))²\n\n⇒ ( (2)/(11) )⁻²⁸ ⁺ ²\n\n⇒ ( (2)/(11) )⁻²⁶\n\nNow equate the powers from both sides:\n\n( (2)/(11) )⁻²⁶ = ( (2)/(11) )⁹m ⁺⁹\n\n⇒ -26 = -(9m + 9)\n\n⇒ 26 = -9m - 9\n\n⇒ 26 + 9 = -9m\n\n⇒ 35 = -9m\n\n⇒ m = -35/9\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**",
